# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
#
# RDR-9: the map comes back after the reader's full screen, and the Tab
# that opens it was not spent while it was away (#332).
# The reader's give-back asks the program to compose the adventuring
# screen, whose roster repaint is drawn over the automap's own panel;
# while a batch of calls into the program runs the engine offers no
# points at all (`seam.h`), so neither point the automap watches its
# cells with can see it. The give-back says so itself now
# (`automap_state::note_panel_painted_over()`) and the map's next arrival
# draws it again over the composed screen, the ordering #303 settled.
# A single leg: `N` reaches the program in a seam-off run (#234), and Tab
# is the automap's, so a seam-off run has no map to compare against.
# Driven by hand on the shorter boot (#291): 121 frames held still, 2
# given back, both `equal` lines at 181 pixels differing, all on the bar.

about the automap comes back after the journal's full screen, and Tab still works
kind single
program START.EXE
both code-wheel
seam automap
seam journal
until 280000000
every 25

# Slot C, the city, and the party's own command bar. Then Tab for the map,
# `Notes` for the empty log, which takes the whole screen just as a full
# one does, and `E` for the way out. Then Tab twice: the first must take
# the map away and the second must bring it back, which is the half of this
# a stale open flag gets wrong.
key L@7550
key C@7800
key Tab@8900
key N@9600
key E@10400
key Tab@11000
key Tab@11600

# The bar row, excepted rather than owned: the give-back injects a space to
# make the menu-bar routine return and draw itself again, and the routine
# draws itself with the highlight at its first command (#234).
rect bar 0,190,319,199

# The map, up and holding still with nothing pressed.
same 9000-9575

# The log, settled over it. It is painted a few rows an arrival by the
# program's own routines, about 130 frames for a listing (#305), so this
# starts after the paint rather than in it.
same 9775-10375

# The map back, and holding still again.
same 10600-10975

# And back once more after the two Tabs.
same 11625-13000

# The whole of #332, as two frames. The map is up in both, the roster is
# under it in both, and the viewport, status line and ornaments are the
# program's own in both. Before the change the runner said `frame 10600 is
# not frame 9000 again: 1633 pixels differ, box 136,16,311,62`, and those
# 1,633 were still there at 11,400, after the first Tab.
equal 9000 10600 bar

# And the key was not spent: Tab took the map away and Tab brought it back,
# so the screen after them is the screen before them.
equal 9000 12200 bar
